// B1 course (A2 → B1 roadmap), module 8 „Õppimine ja kool” (a2b1-036…040), stage B1-.
// Lesson template v4 (owner 2026-10-22, docs/COURSE_DESIGN_COMMUNICATIVE.md §12). One storyline: an autumn when the
// whole family and the office learn — Oskar (9) in grade 3 of his new school, Sofia on an evening Estonian course,
// Anna before a Finnish exam, Markus on an English course at work, Liis as the calm helper and grandmother Helgi (a
// teacher) with advice by phone. The module's goal, said on the first sheet: at the end the learner chooses a course
// and writes an application to it (039 Kasuta).
// B1 grammar of the module: verb government (rektsioon — huvituma millest, osalema milles, aru saama millest,
// rääkima millest, mõtlema millele, sõltuma millest, harjuma millega, abi paluma kellelt, õppima kelle juures,
// valmistuma milleks): taught in 036 (notice, rule table, forms, rewriting, the meeting), used again in 039 (a
// learner's problem, the polite request, the application).
//   036 the parent–teacher meeting about Oskar, his essay; Grandma Helgi's advice on the phone, the class teacher's
//       letter; a new girl in Oskar's class — her mother asks Sofia for help and writes to the teacher.
//   037 Anna's exam plan (ma- or da-infinitive), a chat with Liis; Sofia's homework at the course; the office starts a
//       lunch-time learning club — find a day, agree the rules, write the notice.
//   038 Anna is always tired — a coffee-break talk (sest, kuna, seepärast); why adults learn (a survey), a letter to
//       Helgi; the language school's feedback call and the feedback form.
//   039 Markus fell behind (a chat with Liis, Natalja's story); his teacher's voice message, polite requests, his
//       letter; the module project: three courses, Helgi's advice, a talk with an adviser, the application.
// Lesson 5 (040) is the module's mini Harno A2 exam and the second mid-term check (unchanged). The v3 file is in
// archive/v3/b1/module08.js, the v1 file (Harjuta + Kasuta only) in archive/v1/b1/module08.js.
